---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<Layout title="Disclaimer — Calculator Street" description="Disclaimer: Calculator Street provides estimates only; verify with professionals and local codes.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 py-6 max-md:px-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Disclaimer" }]} />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] pt-6">
      <h1 class="text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-mute">Last updated: September 4, 2026</p>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-6 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 text-sm leading-6 text-body dark:bg-canvas">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Estimates only</h2>
        <p>All calculators on Calculator Street provide estimates only. Materials, densities, coverage rates, prices, labor, waste factors, and yields vary by location, supplier, product, batch, site conditions, and project specifics. Always confirm quantities, costs, and methods with your supplier and contractor before ordering or building.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Not professional advice</h2>
        <p>Nothing on this site is professional construction, engineering, architectural, or financial advice. For structural, roofing, foundation, retaining wall, load-bearing, electrical, plumbing, or code questions, consult a licensed professional. Do not rely solely on calculator outputs for safety-critical decisions.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">No guarantee of accuracy</h2>
        <p>We strive for accuracy with hand-verified formulas, manufacturer yields (e.g., 80-lb concrete = 0.60 ft³), and cited densities (pea 1.35, crushed 1.40, limestone 1.60 tons/yd³ vs scale-house averages; roof multiplier √(pitch²+144)/12). However, we do not guarantee results. Field factors like compaction (TxDOT 15–25%), moisture, spillage, and irregular shapes affect real needs.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Use at your own risk</h2>
        <p>Use of calculators is at your own risk. You are responsible for verifying measurements, adding appropriate waste (we suggest 10% rectangles, 15% curves/hips — adjust per job), and complying with local building codes and permits. We are not liable for over- or under-ordering, cost overruns, rework, delays, or structural failures. See <a href="/terms/" class="text-link underline">Terms</a> for liability limits.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">External links & sources</h2>
        <p>We cite public sources like TxDOT compaction guides and CPSC playground safety for context. Those sources may change; we link for reference but do not control third-party content. Verify current codes with your local authority.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Ads & affiliates</h2>
        <p>We show Google AdSense ads (see <a href="/privacy/" class="text-link underline">Privacy</a>). We do not participate in affiliate programs that affect calculator results. If we add affiliate links in the future, we will disclose them clearly.</p>

        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Contact</h2>
        <p>Found an error? Email <a href="mailto:hello@calculatorst.com" class="text-link underline">hello@calculatorst.com</a> with the calculator URL, your inputs, expected vs actual, and source. We fix verified errors promptly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
